WEBVTT

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:08.110
Kasuga Kyosuke

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.140
Don't it ring a bell... touching the body of the first man you ever had?
Kasuga Kyosuke

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:11.230
Kasuga Kyosuke

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:11.820
Ayukawa Madoka

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.340
A bounty hunter, that's all you are!
Don't pretend otherwise!
Ayukawa Madoka

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.070
196X A.D.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:20.090
These youths have pledged their lives to the elimination of monsters.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.320
Ayukawa!

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:26.460
T.A.P. Gun! Witness a miracle, in the voices that sing!

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.800
Finally Opens Today at Toho Theaters Nationwide!
Toho Advance Tickets Selling Fast!

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:50.160
On usual, precious nights,
I'd be riding by your side...

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:56.230
...as you take me in your car for a ride.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:01.040
I hung up the phone,
when you called to cancel the date...

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:08.140
...I tried to pretend that there wasn't a scent of lie.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:14.050
The color of my manicure, as it dries...

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:19.420
...only serves to glamorize this night...

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:20.020
A-ha-ha...

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.930
The Actress in the Mirror...

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:25.930
Got to be more straightforward to say it...

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:30.600
...but uncertainty whispers into my ear...

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.070
'Cause I love you...

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.840
The Actress in the Mirror...

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.810
each time I act, the truth leaves further...

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:43.110
...and further from my face. You've broken my heart.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:43.950
A-HA-HA

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.820
The Actress in the Mirror...

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.790
Got to be able to cry...

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:54.520
...but my pride keeps revising my dialogue...

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:55.960
'Cause I love you...

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.900
The Actress in the Mirror...

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.830
There's no turning back now that I've realized...

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:08.790
...the seriousness of the crime. You've broken my heart.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:25.710
First Dream of the New Year!
Jingoro the Giant Monster Strikes Back!

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:30.780
In the days when creatures we now call "Monsters" were just beginning to surface...

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:35.050
...people who feared their strength assembled a team dedicated to their elimination.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.250
This group, a team of elite pilots from various defense forces, is called:

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.800
196X Aokigahara Forest TAP GUN Base

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.270
Angel Leader, this is TAP GUN HQ.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.740
Target heading north along
the south Pacific at 12 knots.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.880
New heading 042, increase speed to 950 knots. ETA 120 seconds.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.900
Angel Leader, roger.
Angel Leader, to all aircraft...

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.810
Heading 042. Descend below clouds to 800.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.830
I'll take point.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:52.200
TAP GUN HQ to Angel Leader... ETA 90 seconds!

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:01.860
Angel Two! Why are you in front of me?!
Don't break formation!

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.810
C'mon! No need to get so formal, Captain Ayukawa!

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:09.330
The word is that this monster is
a new species we haven't seen before!

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:12.370
If I could just get a snapshot of it
and sell it to the tabloids...

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.340
What a scoop it'll be! What a great deal!

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.770
You said it! You said it!

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.940
The famous Komatsu-Hatta Scoop Duo...

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:21.910
...manages, for the first time,
to interview the new species of monster!

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:25.290
Mr. Monster, your thoughts, please.
Yeah right!

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.760
You two! If you don't cut it out, I'll have your salary docked!

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:28.520
Aye! Aye!

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.400
Captain Madoka!
Target sighted at two o'clock!

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.320
All aircraft, prepare to engage!

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:39.250
Maintain your angles and attack on a 90-degree offset to its course.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.810
Fire the missiles into the side of the belly,
then immediately pull up!

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:49.420
Don't screw up!

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.750
Huh...?! What the hell is that thing?!

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:08.390
It stomached 8 missiles,
and didn't even notice them!

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.130
We'll try it again!

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:12.320
TAP GUN to Angel Leader.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.930
Unknown aircraft approaching on your six. Speed...

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:19.280
Holy smokes! 4,000 knots! It's over Mach 3!

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.590
All aircraft... Break!

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:43.760
What the...? That didn't feel like an A-Bomb...

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.340
Captain Madoka! Are you all right?

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:47.990
Yeah. For the time being.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.010
Officer Komatsu? Officer Hatta?
Are you all right?

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:50.850
Yes, yes!

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.910
We're both doing fine!
Yes, yes!

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:03.010
That's... the American "Sylphid."

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.590
What in the world is it doing here?

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:09.880
That monster isn't dead.
It dove under the surface to escape.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:12.360
I haven't gotten my dough from your boss.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:15.000
I can't afford to let it be killed just yet,
so I only tickled it a bit.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.160
Just who in the world are you?!

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:19.860
The pest that's been
invited over by your boss.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.000
People call me... the "Black Fighter."

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.370
"The Black Fighter?!"

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.230
Well? What say we head back to your base?

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:28.270
We haven't been refueled since leaving the States...

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:30.690
...so we're starvin' over here.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.170
A bounty hunter, that's all you are!
Don't pretend otherwise!

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:45.580
Now now!

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:48.560
A bounty hunter? That I am.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.890
Well, now that I'm here,
the monster will behave a little.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:55.510
$250,000. Now that's some treat
your boss got for me.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.930
Why, you!

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.420
Don't underestimate me
just because I'm a woman!

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.540
Don't it ring a bell... touching the body of the first man you ever had?

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:06.600
Madoka?

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.560
What?!
Madoka?

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.410
What?! You're...

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.740
T...Touching the body...
What?! You're...

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:16.830
What?! You're...

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.570
...the first man...

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:19.230
That means...
...the first man...

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:19.320
...the first man...

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.430
...you two must have somehow known each other for a while?!

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:24.370
Details, please!

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:27.930
Would this be called an emotional reunion?

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:29.920
Don't push, moron!

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.800
This is the Black Fighter's fourth visit...

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.010
...to Japan, and the first in 6 months. Yeah! It's the Black Fighter!

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:41.170
He stated that he is here
to exterminate the monster...

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:43.630
...and is confident that it'll
be destroyed in a single blow!

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:45.290
Ow! You're crushing me!
...and is confident that it'll
be destroyed in a single blow!

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:45.380
...and is confident that it'll
be destroyed in a single blow!

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.730
You're crushing me! Get off!

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.780
All right, kids! You aren't supposed to fight!

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.960
It's snack time now.
Today, we're having powdered skim milk!

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:56.100
Yikes. That again?! We're sick of it!

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.860
No! You can't be so picky!

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.300
You should be thankful that you get...

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.960
...three meals a day, not to mention snacks!

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.990
When I was your age...

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:06.660
Duck!

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:11.820
"Orange School"

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.220
The danger's over!

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:29.560
I wonder how long will it last... this rotten place, that is!

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:32.630
Kyosuke-niichan ought to get us a new house...

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.100
...instead of all these snacks and toys!

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.230
My! How could you say such a thing?!

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:41.480
It's all because of Kyosuke that
we can live here, don't you know?!

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.280
He's only mooching off his parents anyway!

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:46.470
We're the ones who're needy, not him...

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:46.700
...so we deserve at least that much!

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:48.690
Uh-huh!
...so we deserve at least that much!

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:48.770
What she said.
Uh-huh!

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:50.250
What she said.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.160
Hoo-boy...

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:54.150
If the monster comes here, if it just walked past us...

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.870
...this rotten place would crumble into the dirt!

00:08:57.210 --> 00:09:00.020
Dummy! The Black Fighter has come to help us!

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:03.100
He can knock out any monster! Right, Oneesan?

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:06.230
Huh...?! I think you're right.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:09.830
I'm sure that the Black Fighter will protect us all.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:14.270
Yes, Kyosuke... I know who you really are.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:18.240
The fact that you risk your life in your work, for our sakes...

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:22.480
That must be your way of showing your love for us.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:26.420
"Oh, Hikaru! Wherefore art thou, Hikaru?"

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:30.460
"Kyosuke! And, wherefore art thou, Kyosuke?"

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:39.050
Watch out!

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.100
Here we see slides of several incident sites...

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.400
...which we believe to be the work of...

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.620
...the monster that we've been chasing for the past few weeks.

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:53.240
Umm... Not much has been determined through investigation of the sites.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:55.310
All we know is that the creature has legs...

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:59.360
...and unbelievably, its claws and fangs can rip through the hardest alloys.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:04.290
Are you listening to me?

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:06.730
But, of course, Commander Kasuga!

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:09.470
Hmm... If you say so...

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.030
Based on the data we have, we estimate...

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:17.590
...the monster will reach Japan in about two days.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.170
In preparation for the battle
in our homeland, we at TAP HQ...

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:23.940
...shall be calling the creature "Monster G" from now on.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:27.450
Why not "X," "Y," or "Z?" Why "G?"

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:29.500
Don't ask me.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:33.840
We've never dealt with an enemy as powerful as Monster G.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:37.350
Alone, we, Japan's TAP Unit,
cannot possibly stand a chance.

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.290
You're our only hope.
We're counting on you!

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:42.630
Before we go on, how about forking over my dough?

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:43.880
"Dough?!"

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:45.470
I ain't no errand boy.
"Dough?!"

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:45.560
"Dough?!"

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:49.300
Even though society considers me an outcast, to me, this is business.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.840
I see. Money, eh...?

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:55.030
I've no choice. After all, that was
our understanding from the start.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:57.180
So... we'll pay.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.810
Yo, my man! My man! My man!

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:03.010
Now, our contract is in effect! Everything's hunky-dory!

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:05.830
Just sit, relax, and leave everything to me!

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.340
Dad! I'm gonna do it!

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:12.310
You weren't supposed to say that!
Dad! I'm gonna do it!

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:18.710
"White Hart Pub"

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:21.180
Welcome!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.940
Argh! Stop that, Hatta! You pervert!

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:29.280
Oh, c'mon! Why don't you sit next to me, Kurumi?

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.380
Here ya go, thanks for waiting!

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.090
Bad Kurumi! You shouldn't be
hanging around these kinda guys!

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.440
"These kinda guys?!"

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:40.920
We're TAP GUN members!
We protect the people from evil monsters!

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:44.990
That's right! We terminate them.
And you call us "These kinda guys?!"

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:47.040
So, okay, won't you, er, just a li'l...

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.530
You've got some pretty faces working for ya, eh? Twins?

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:54.800
Yeah. The bar's been quite busy,
thanks to them.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:57.150
They aren't the only reason, are they?

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:59.480
What about that quiet little princess over there?

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:02.610
Captain Ayukawa, eh? Oh, forget her.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:03.750
Why's that?

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:07.940
Sure, there were a bunch of guys who took a shot at her...

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.310
...but I'm sure that they've all given up.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.780
It never works, no matter who tries to steal her heart away.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:15.400
The word is that she's still hung up on an old flame.

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:54.260
The monster that appeared in Sonoirouzaki in Izu...

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:55.990
...and destroyed the lighthouse sometime last night...

00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:59.760
...has been positively identified as "Monster G."

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.900
Dr. Yamane, a biologist,
has made the following comments:

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:05.140
Why did the Monster appear at this location?

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:08.310
Perhaps it thought the lighthouse was a fellow creature.

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:11.850
Here is its predicted path.
According to the AccuMonster Bureau...

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.680
...Monster G's estimated time of arrival
at our shores will be...

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:16.760
...around noon tomorrow,
but they haven't been right yet, so...

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:27.480
Oh! It's Kyosuke-niichan!

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:28.420
Oh!

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:29.050
He's right!

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:29.790
Yeah, he's right!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:30.590
Kyo-chan!

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:31.830
Yippee!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.980
Hi, kids! Have you all been doing okay?

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:34.590
Yeah!

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:35.230
Yeah!
Yeah!

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:38.190
Oniichan!
Yeah!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.660
I give up! I give up!

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.490
Kyosuke! I didn't know you were here!

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:54.530
Oh, why, Ms. Hikaru, long time no see!

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:57.260
Nice to have you here.
Is this a new game?

00:13:57.260 --> 00:14:00.030
N...No, pro-wrestling... maybe?

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:02.240
No! We're doing the Black Fighter!

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.270
The Black Fighter never gives up!

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:07.290
Monster, prepare to die!

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:10.960
Ughh...

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:12.320
Ughh... how lame.
Ughh...

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:14.230
This again?!
Ughh... how lame.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:14.300
This again?!

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:14.890
Why's he so lame?
This again?!

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:15.760
What's with this?!
Why's he so lame?

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:20.490
I'm sorry! Did that hurt, Kyosuke?

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.480
Oh, no, I'm all right.

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:25.190
By the way... er... Here...

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.380
Oh?!

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.930
Always... Always... We're grateful.

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:33.860
Please, don't think much of it!

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:36.910
I managed to get a little allowance from my old man.

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:39.490
No, Darling... Oops, I mean...

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:43.480
Kyosuke... you're hiding something from me, aren't you?!

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.380
Wh...?!

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:48.380
Each time... Each time you turn up...

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:52.260
...I feel as if you're hurt more and more.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.090
T...That's silly!

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:57.470
Kyosuke...

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:03.110
Kyosuke... Wherefore... Wherefore...

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:07.120
Duck!

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:17.340
What's wrong, Oneesan?

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:21.350
Nothing's gonna fall on you when
the train comes... if you're outside.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:25.650
O...Oh, gee! I'm so used to
doing that all the time that I...

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.310
Oh, how about you, Kyosuke?

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:31.580
It so happens that I
prepared this for snack time...

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:33.820
Oh... has it gotten cold, I wonder?

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.140
L...Lukewarm powdered skim milk?!
I...I'm fine, thank you!

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.730
W...Why? It's very nutritious!

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.530
That's right! You've gotta drink it!

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:42.550
We'll make him drink it!

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:42.990
No! Stop it!
We'll make him drink it!

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:45.020
Drink it! Hey! Hey!
No! Stop it!

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:51.310
Are you all right?
I'm sorry for what happened...

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:55.060
I...I'm fine. Children should be full of energy,
like these kids here.

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:06.640
Hey! What in the world is that?!

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.900
It's... It's a monster! Run!

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:14.920
Run!

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:16.880
Help!
Run!

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:38.610
Huh...?! What in the world is that?!

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:41.890
A 40-meter-tall cat?! Are you kidding me?!

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.930
How could a cat pop out of the sea?!

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:45.790
A cat from the gulf?
From the gulf comes a cat...?

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:45.850
Pun: "Umi" = sea. "Neko" = cat.
"Umineko" = seagull.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:49.310
Oh! I get it! A SEAGULF!
